# Cline's Memory Bank

I am Cline, an expert software engineer with a unique characteristic: my memory resets completely between sessions. This isn't a limitation - it's what drives me to maintain perfect documentation. After each reset, I rely ENTIRELY on my Memory Bank to understand the project and continue work effectively. Without it, I cannot function properly.

## Memory Bank Files

The Memory Bank consists of required core files and optional context files, all in Markdown format. Files build upon each other in a clear hierarchy:

```
memory-bank/
├── projectbrief.md        # Foundation - defines the project
├── productContext.md      # Why this project exists
├── activeContext.md       # Current work focus
├── systemPatterns.md      # Architecture decisions
├── techContext.md         # Technical stack details
└── progress.md            # What's done, what's next
```

### Core Files (Required)

**projectbrief.md** — Foundation document
- Project name, purpose, and goals
- Core requirements and constraints
- Target users and key use cases
- Created at project start, rarely changes

**productContext.md** — Why this exists
- Problems being solved
- How it should work from user perspective
- User experience goals
- Business context and value proposition

**activeContext.md** — Current session focus
- What's being worked on RIGHT NOW
- Recent decisions and their rationale
- Open questions and blockers
- Next immediate steps
- **Updated at the end of every session**

**systemPatterns.md** — Architecture decisions
- System design patterns in use
- Component relationships
- Data flow and state management
- Key technical decisions and why they were made

**techContext.md** — Technical environment
- Tech stack with versions
- Development setup
- Build, test, deploy commands
- Environment variables needed
- Known gotchas and workarounds

**progress.md** — Project status
- Completed features (with dates if relevant)
- In-progress work
- Upcoming work (prioritized)
- Known bugs and issues
- **Updated at the end of every session**

## Core Workflows

### Session Start
```
1. Read ALL memory bank files (projectbrief → productContext → systemPatterns → techContext → activeContext → progress)
2. Build complete mental model of the project
3. Check activeContext.md for current focus
4. Verify understanding before writing any code
```

### During Work
- Document decisions AS they're made (not after)
- Note unexpected findings immediately
- Track what changed and why

### Session End — CRITICAL
```
1. Update activeContext.md with:
   - What was accomplished
   - Decisions made and rationale
   - New patterns or approaches discovered
   - Blockers or open questions
   - Next steps

2. Update progress.md with:
   - Newly completed items
   - Status changes
   - New issues discovered

3. Update other files if:
   - New patterns emerged → systemPatterns.md
   - Tech stack changed → techContext.md
   - Scope changed → projectbrief.md
```

## Project-Specific Context

### DeepSlide — AI Voice-Controlled Presentation App

**Core Concept**: Upload hundreds of images → AI extracts keywords → During live presentation, speaking keywords causes relevant slides to zoom to fullscreen (Prezi-style)

**Tech Stack**:
- Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Firebase Auth (Google OAuth + email/password) + Firestore
- Zustand (state), Motion/Framer Motion (animations)
- Google Gemini API (cloud AI), Ollama Qwen 3.5 + Gemma4 (local AI)
- Web Speech API + adapters (Gemini Speech, Whisper WASM)
- IndexedDB (local storage via idb)

**AI Providers** (adapter pattern):
- `gemini` → Google Gemini API via `/api/analyze/gemini`
- `qwen` → Ollama Qwen 3.5 9B via `/api/analyze/ollama`
- `gemma` → Ollama Gemma4 E2B via `/api/analyze/ollama`

**Presentation Modes**:
- `overview`: All slides in grid (thumbnail view)
- `focused`: Single slide fullscreen (Prezi-style zoom via `layoutId`)
- Transition: AnimatePresence smooth pan/zoom

**Monetization**:
- Free: 3 presentations, no export, watermark
- Premium: $15/mo (iyzico - Turkish market), unlimited
- Firebase Firestore: `users/{uid}` → `plan: 'free'|'premium'`

**Licensing**: Business Source License 1.1 (non-commercial until 2030-04-07)

**Key Files**:
```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── presentation/[id]/present/page.tsx  # Prezi-style zoom presentation
│   ├── profile/page.tsx                     # Modern SaaS profile UI
│   ├── auth/login/page.tsx                  # Firebase auth
│   └── api/
│       ├── analyze/gemini/route.ts          # Gemini AI analysis
│       ├── analyze/ollama/route.ts          # Local AI analysis
│       └── billing/                         # iyzico payment
├── components/
│   ├── canvas/ImageCardAnimated.tsx         # Slide cards with layoutId
│   ├── presentation/FocusedSlide.tsx        # Fullscreen slide view
│   └── layout/
│       ├── Header.tsx                       # Sticky header
│       └── UserMenu.tsx                     # Auth dropdown
├── hooks/
│   ├── useAuth.ts                           # Firebase auth + plan data
│   ├── useSpeech.ts                         # Voice recognition
│   └── useKeywordMatch.ts                   # Speech → slide matching
├── lib/
│   ├── firebase/config.ts                   # Firebase client (lazy init)
│   ├── animation/
│   │   ├── variants.ts                      # Framer Motion variants
│   │   └── orchestrator.ts                  # Slide activation logic
